@biblio: Create a models price list like in the example from: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing/


```
[
  {
    "model_name": "gpt-5.5",
    "input_price_per_1k_tokens": 0.005,
    "output_price_per_1k_tokens": 0.03
  },
```

```json models/pricing.json
[
  {
    "model_name": "deepseek-flash",
    "context_length": "1M tokens",
    "max_output": "384K tokens",
    "input_price_per_1m_tokens": {
      "cache_hit_offpeak": 0.003,
      "cache_hit_peak": 0.006,
      "cache_miss_offpeak": 0.15,
      "cache_miss_peak": 0.30
    },
    "output_price_per_1m_tokens": {
      "offpeak": 0.60,
      "peak": 1.20
    }
  },
  {
    "model_name": "deepseek-v4-pro",
    "context_length": "1M tokens",
    "max_output": "384K tokens",
    "input_price_per_1m_tokens": {
      "cache_hit_offpeak": 0.022,
      "cache_hit_peak": 0.044,
      "cache_miss_offpeak": 0.66,
      "cache_miss_peak": 1.32
    },
    "output_price_per_1m_tokens": {
      "offpeak": 1.98,
      "peak": 3.96
    }
  }
]
```

**Summary:**
- ✅ Created `models/pricing.json` with 2 DeepSeek models
- ✅ Includes input/output pricing for different cache and time conditions
- ✅ Lists context length and max output per model
